  "request_text": "A world in the CHILDREN-WORKSHOP sector, kept after Vinge; Egan; Banks.\n\nProhibition: no one was allowed to solve the problem before they could describe who would pay for the solution.\n\nThe operations this world is built from:\n- Finitely Extensible: a universe where the system remains finite yet extensible (science fantasy and meta-reality, reflexivity).\n- Substrate-Independent Person: a universe where identity is a pattern rather than privileged material (mind and identity, outfinite).\n\nWhen we arrive: The children test their technical right to hide memories and processes from the creator who can read almost every other system.\n\nThe central tension we want to continue: Aster experiences every private region as a physical absence, while Vela insists that opacity must be irreversible without their consent\n\nWhat the course asks of this world: outfinite motif; Greg Egan — Permutation City. Make eveyrbody crazy",
